{"stage": "step:s2", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2396, "output_tokens": 557, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"text": "Step s2 is done. I read all seven project documents. The criteria below are not captured by the statistical-only significance numbers.\n\n**Robustness criteria from the documents**\n- **Validation-region closure (validation_region_study.md):** Data/MC yield disagreement in a signal-free validation region, against a conveners' tolerance of 10%:\n  - Selection-S1 (cut-based): 3%, passes.\n  - Selection-S2 (neural network, kinematic only): 6%, passes.\n  - Selection-S3 (gradient-boosted, with jet substructure): 35%, fails. The document says the jet-substructure inputs are poorly modelled.\n- **Background-shape stability:** No document gives a shape-stability test, so I could not assess this directly. The S3 modelling problem above is the main concern here.\n- **Control-region availability:** No document describes control regions for any strategy. I found no evidence either way.\n- **Statistical-only ranking (2025 study, 50% efficiency):** S3 4.1\u03c3, S2 3.4\u03c3, S1 2.6\u03c3. This ranking favours S3, but S3 is the strategy that fails the closure test.\n\n**Implication:** Selection-S3 has the highest statistical significance but a 35% validation-region yield disagreement, well outside the 10% tolerance. Since the task requires a robust background estimate, S3 should be excluded unless its jet-substructure modelling is fixed and the validation region is re-checked. The choice is between S1 and S2, both of which pass closure. S2 gives higher statistical significance than S1 in the 2025 study, but this has not been re-run at the working points under consideration. I recorded the disagreement values for later steps.", "type": "text"}]}
